SUMMARY:LATE ADD SALE: Observational Watercolor: Painting Produce (6 sessi
 on series) — Sebastopol Center For the Arts\, California
DTSTART:20260823T000000
DTEND:20260824T000000
UID:82bf81ea9e0d935c012f8256a2928a42@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Sale\n      \n\n\n\n\n\nObservational Watercolor: Painting Pro
 duce (6 session series)\n\n\n          Sale Price:\n        \n        $220
 .00 \n        \n          Original Price:\n        \n\n          $330.00\n
         \n\nThis 6 session series meets Midday on Sundays\, starting Augus
 t 9th. August 9th\, 16th\, 23rd (skipping August 30th)\, September 6th\, 1
 3th\, 20th from 1:00pm to 4:00pm. $300.00 + $30.00 Materials Fee Special L
 ate Add Offer:Join August 23rd\, for $100.00 off the registration fee! $20
 0 + $20.00 Materials Fee Age restricted to 18+In this six session course\,
  students will learn a unique approach to watercolor\, intended to address
  the frustration that many feel with this challenging medium. The class wi
 ll focus on strengthening one’s observational skills\, while learning a 
 watercolor technique that teaches the artist to see value and color. Thro
 ughout the course\, we will work on 3 paintings\, progressing through simp
 ler to more complex forms. With a mix of demonstrations and individualized
  instruction\, students of all experience levels will develop new skills a
 nd have a meaningful creative experience. Our unifying subject will be se
 asonal produce - fruits\, vegetables\, and herbs. These subjects are great
  for beginners and master painters alike\; their organic shapes are forgiv
 ing drawing subjects\, but their beauty can be a muse for life. Instructo
 r Hannah Day is a passionate produce lover and botanical painter and will 
 share her unique approach to rendering botanicals. This class will work fr
 om life\, practicing observational drawing\, in addition to watercolor tec
 hnique. With six class sessions\, participants will have the opportunity 
 to develop their skills and build muscle memory with a medium that often f
 eels like it has a mind of its own. Beginning artists and repeat students
  are welcome.About the Instructor: Hannah Day received her BA in Visual Ar
 ts with an emphasis on drawing and printmaking from University of San Dieg
 o\, then attended University of Hawaii at Manoa to receive her MFA in prin
 tmaking. Hannah’s etchings have been internationally shown and collected
 \, but her art practice also includes paper cutting\, graphite\, and water
 color. She has taught all ages in many mediums. These days\, Hannah primar
 ily teaches watercolor\, observational drawing\, and paper cutting. You ca
 n view her work at www.hannahdrawstrees.com\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\
 n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n          \n            \n             
  \n                Add to cart
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA 
 95472
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/observational-watercolor-pain
 ting-produce-6-session-series
X-SOURCE:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
