END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Collage Your Story with Catherine Cruz  — Sebastopol Center For 
 the Arts\, California
DTSTART:20260829T000000
DTEND:20260830T000000
UID:7648589322e0208442181253a864c4bc@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Collage Your Story with Catherine Cruz - August 29th\n\n  \n  
   \n      \n        \n          $130.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nSat
 urday\, August 29th\, 2026\; 11:00am - 3:00pmFee: $115 + $15 materials fee
 Ages 16 and up\; Located in Dining Room at SebArtsJoin French-American col
 lage artist Catherine Cruz for a special\, personalized workshop designed 
 just for you! The word collage comes from the French verb coller\, meaning
  "to glue\," and is all about merging various materials to tell a visual s
 tory. Much like our lives\, which are shaped by countless moments and expe
 riences\, collage pieces bring together fragments that reveal hidden conne
 ctions and untold narratives. In this class\, you’ll reflect on what mat
 ters most to you and how that can be expressed through art. Catherine will
  help you release the need for perfection and trust your creative instinct
 s. By the end of the workshop\, you’ll not only have a finished artwork 
 but also a deeper connection to your creative potential and a renewed love
  for the art of collage.What you’ll learn: Creative ways to incorporate 
 your personal story in your artMethods for sourcing interesting collage pa
 persTechniques for crafting textured\, multi-layered collagesStrategies fo
 r refining your composition Materials:Participants must purchase and brin
 g the following items – Instructor will not provide panels for this clas
 s:One 12”x12” cradled wood panel\, either ¾” thick or 1 ½” thick
  – panel can be purchased locally at RileyStreet Art Supply or online at
  Blick.com – Do not use a canvas.Apron or painting shirtNitrile gloves i
 f you have sensitive skinBrown bag lunch and beverageAny collage papers yo
 u would like to use – see below RequirementsPlease bring your own paper
 s to personalize your artwork like ephemera that represents your life or a
  certain period of time\, copies of photos\, old letters\, book pages\, pa
 pers from memorable experiences or travels\, or documents that hold meanin
 g. If you’re not comfortable using these documents\, you should make las
 er color copies of them. You will not be able to use anything printed on g
 lossy paper or photo paper so it is best to make laser copies of your phot
 ographs. Inkjet prints do not work with this process.About the instructor:
  Catherine Cruz is a French-American artist whose work is informed by text
 ures and patterns created by the passing of time and the effects of the na
 tural elements on the built environment.  She holds a Bachelor of Science
  in interior design and she worked in the field of architectural design an
 d green building certification for over 25 years.  She has taught collage
  and mixed media workshops in the Bay Area and in France since 2019\, and 
 this is her fifth year at the Sebastopol Center for the Arts.  Her studio
  is located in Sebastopol and she participates in Art Trails Open Studios.
   You may contact Catherine at beyouartstudio@gmail.com.  Check out Cath
 erine’s other classes here:  https://wwws.sebarts.org/visual-arts-class
 es. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    
       \n            \n              \n                Add to cart
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA 
 95472
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/collage-your-story-with-cathe
 rine-cruz-1
X-SOURCE:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
